Doom for Inferno — build plan
=============================

Goal: run shareware Doom (doom1.wad) under hosted emu, engine rewritten
in Limbo.  Reference spec: doomgeneric's 5-function platform seam
(DG_Init, DG_DrawFrame, DG_SleepMs, DG_GetTicksMs, DG_GetKey) — we port
the seam to Inferno and translate the engine body C -> Limbo.

Platform services available in-tree (verified):
  blit      Draw->Image.writepixels(dst, r, data), module/draw.m:190;
            data must match the screen's native format — hosted emu
            is 32bpp XRGB32 (emu/port/win-x11a.c forces depth 32)
  screen    Display.allocate(nil) then draw/writepixels on
            display.image (appl/cmd/wish.b path); no Tk, no wm needed
  clock     Sys->millisec(), Sys->sleep(), module/sys.m:141,153
  keys      /dev/keyboard + /dev/pointer readers
            (appl/cmd/wish.b spawn pattern)
  audio     /dev/audio + /dev/audioctl, enc pcm, rate 11025
            (emu/port/audio-tbls.c — exactly Doom's SFX rate)

Layout
------
  wad.m/wad.b      WAD container loader (module, reusable)
  video.m/video.b  XRGB32 framebuffer -> emu screen blit (module)
  rend.m/rend.b    renderer: palette, colormap, flats, textures,
                   vanilla column/span drawers (module)
  map.m/map.b      map geometry: vertices, sectors, sides, lines,
                   things as adts; shared ref Sectors (module)
  view.m/view.b    world-view renderer: BSP walk, seg clip, wall
                   columns, two-sided upper/lower (module)
  doom.b           main command; grows with each milestone
  doom1.wad        shareware IWAD (data, place in $ROOT or pass path)
  PLAN             this file

