            was correct, so texture coords slid the wrong way - shear that
            grows with the column's lateral offset (zero at default view,
            worst at the screen edges on rotation).  REPEAT-MISTAKE NOTE:
            individual pieces (basexscale sign, origin single-fixedmul,
            distscale=1/cos, yslope) were each "verified" against vanilla
            in earlier passes and shear persisted, because the origin and
            step were never checked against EACH OTHER in reduced form.
            Always reduce the raw vanilla lines to the port's vsin/vcos
            terms in one place and compare BOTH the origin and the step
            together before touching anything else.
